# `makefiles/terra.mk` keeps REPORT_PATH at its default `build/reports/`, which `common`
# already covers. These are the two things its test tiers write BESIDES their reports.

# `terraform init` vendors provider binaries and module sources next to the module it
# initialises, so the directory appears at whatever depth the tree has: `test` /
# `test-terra-test` run it once per module (`terraform/terra-test/run.sh` ->
# `modules/*/.terraform/`) and `test-validate` once per root module
# (`terraform/validate/run.sh` -> `stacks/*/.terraform/`). Unanchored on purpose, which is
# also what every published Terraform `.gitignore` does.
#
# `.terraform.lock.hcl` is deliberately NOT here: it pins provider versions and is meant
# to be committed.
.terraform/

# `terraform/validate/run.sh` points TF_PLUGIN_CACHE_DIR at
# `$(pwd)/build/.terraform-plugin-cache`, inside the checkout on purpose -- Terraform's
# plugin cache is not safe for concurrent use, and `$HOME` is exactly what is shared when
# a self-hosted host runs several agents side by side. It sits under `build/`, NOT under
# `build/reports/`, so `common` does not match it, and it fills with every provider the
# repository uses.
/build/.terraform-plugin-cache/
